.TH "libnvme" 9 "struct nvme_mi_pcie_req_hdr" "November 2026" "API Manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
struct nvme_mi_pcie_req_hdr \- PCIe command request header.
.SH SYNOPSIS
struct nvme_mi_pcie_req_hdr {
.br
.BI "    struct nvme_mi_msg_hdr hdr;"
.br
.BI "    __u8 opcode;"
.br
.BI "    __u8 rsvd;"
.br
.BI "    __le16 ctrlid;"
.br
.BI "    __le32 nmd0, nmd1, nmd2;"
.br
.BI "
};
.br

.SH Members
.IP "hdr" 12
generic MI message header
.IP "opcode" 12
opcode (OPC) for the specific PCIe command
.IP "rsvd" 12
reserved
.IP "ctrlid" 12
Controller ID (CTLID) of the NVMe Controller this command targets
.IP "nmd0" 12
PCIe Request Dword 0 - command specific usage
.IP "nmd1" 12
PCIe Request Dword 1 - command specific usage
.IP "nmd2" 12
PCIe Request Dword 2 - command specific usage
.SH "Description"
Wire format for PCIe command request headers (20 bytes), defined in the
NVMe-MI PCIe Command Set. NMIMT in \fIhdr.nmp\fP is set to NVME_MI_MT_PCIE (4)
by \fBlibnvme_mi_pcie_xfer\fP.
